A||N||5||Monkeyman||Tire size info, please||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-15-2001||05:06 AM||||I know that the stock 15" tire size is 215/60R15.  What is the next lowest profile tire size?  Not a 16" plus 1 size.  225/50?  215/50?  For some reason, I'm getting confused.<P>MM||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||05-15-2001||09:05 AM||||Well, if you do the math, in order to keep the same overall tire height on a 15" wheel, the next step from a 215/60-15 is a 235/55-15, but virtually no one makes this size, so the next closest size is 245/50-15, which may be too big for your stock rims.  They should fit on 7" rims, but most people here wouldn't recommend it.  You could go with 225/50-15's, but they're shorter than the original size and will increase your fender gap - no too much of an issue on a lowered car, but would look pretty silly with stock ride height.  I'm still considering 225/50-15 to replace my 205/60s up front and the 245/50-15 to replace the 215s on the back.  I just haven't decided if I want to try to put that much tire on my stock rims.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Oreif||05-15-2001||10:16 AM||||If your car came with 215/60R14's (SE's, 85 GT's, SC's, etc) the 15" tire size is 225/50R15's. If your car originally had the 215/60R15's, 245/50R15's would give you the same outside diameter but you would need an 8" wheel. (Stock 15" is only 7" wide).<BR>It is usually easier to go up a wheel size to maintain the diameter. (14 to 15, 15 to 16, etc) <P>Here is a link that you can type in the original tire size and the tire size you wish to go to. It will show you the size difference and calculate the speedo error if you went to the different size.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-15-2001||04:53 PM||||Although I own an '85 GT, I currently have 15" rims on her and plan on buying some stock 15" lace rims in the near future.  I'd like some wider/slightly lower profile tires.  I haven't lowered it yet but hope to either later this summer or sometime this fall/winter.  I would go with some 16" rims, but I really like the 15" stockers.  I may just have to stick with the stock size this go 'round and switch to another size once they wear out.  <P>Thanx for the info.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Vader||05-15-2001||10:54 PM||||I've had good luck with 225/50-16s on my roller skate:<P> <IMG SRC="http://homestead.juno.com/jlstrey/files/fiero06.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-16-2001||01:45 AM||||85 GT and 86 SE look the same body wise.<BR>Mine are 225/50R15's. and it's lowered 1.5"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86SE_2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <BR>Got Emblems?||||reg||1
